.policy "pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str" revision 1
.description "Declare a secret on a Pydantic settings class (a password, token, API key, private key) as SecretStr, not str, so printing or dumping the settings never shows it."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. The settings object is the one a process prints, logs or dumps at start-up, and
// `repr()`, `str()`, `model_dump()`, `model_dump_json()` of it, and a ValidationError raised on it, print a `str` field
// in clear. `SecretStr` prints `'**********'` in all of them until `.get_secret_value()` (Pydantic docs, Secret types;
// pydantic-settings docs use SecretStr for credentials). OWASP's Logging Cheat Sheet and CWE-532: never log secrets.
//   class Settings(BaseSettings):
//       SECRET_KEY: str                                   reported
//       SMTP_PASSWORD: str | None = None                  reported
//       OPENAI_API_KEY: Annotated[str, Field(min_length=20)]   reported
//       JWT_SECRET: SecretStr                             not reported: the safe type
//       JWT_TOKEN_AUDIENCE: str = "api"                   not reported: the name ends in what the value is, an audience
//       TOKEN_URL: str = "https://..."                    not reported: the name ends in what the value is, a URL
// What it reads: the fields of a pydantic_settings.BaseSettings class (lib/pydantic's pd_settings, through the run's
// classes in any module), inherited ones included (pd_has_field: a settings base or a BaseModel mixin in another
// file), and the fields of a plain model a settings class holds as a field (`smtp: SmtpConfig`, nested settings),
// whose values the parent's repr and dump print too. A field is reported, once at its declaration, when:
//   - its type is a plain string, alone or with None: resolved, not read as text. Its leaves are the builtin `str`,
//     pydantic's StrictStr or a `constr(...)` call (by their imported symbol), and `None`, through `Optional[...]`,
//     `Union[...]`, `|` and `Annotated[..., ...]` (typing's, by symbol), and through a module-level alias of the
//     run (`PlainStr = str`, `NonEmpty = Annotated[str, Field(min_length=1)]`, imported from another module or not);
//   - its name, or a string `alias=` / `validation_alias=` (`AliasChoices(...)` included) its Field gives, ends in a
//     secret: the name is cut into word parts at `_` and at camel-case humps, case-insensitive, a trailing number
//     dropped, and the last part is password, passwd, secret, token, credential(s), apikey or pepper (`SMTP_PASSWORD`,
//     `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `slackBotToken`, `SENDGRID_APIKEY`), or the last part is key and the part before it is
//     one of those words, api or private, or access after one of those (`SECRET_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`,
//     `GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`, `privateKey`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`). A bare `ACCESS_KEY` (`S3_ACCESS_KEY`) is the
//     access key id, the public half of the pair, whose `SECRET_KEY` is caught: left alone.
// The name is the only signal of what a `str` holds that the engine can decide: the type is `str` either way, and the
// value comes from the environment. So the test is the last word of the name, which says what the value is: a name
// that merely mentions a secret and ends in something else is about the secret, not the secret (`TOKEN_URL`,
// `JWT_TOKEN_AUDIENCE`, `TOKEN_ISSUER`, `PASSWORD_HASH_SCHEME`, `AUTH_TOKEN_COOKIE`, `GITHUB_TOKEN_SCOPES`,
// `SECRET_KEY_FILE`, `API_KEY_NAME`, `CURRENT_HASH_SECRET_ID`), and `TOKENIZER` or `PASSWORDLESS_LOGIN` have no
// secret part at all.
// The message counts the reads of `.NAME` in the run's files: changing the type to SecretStr breaks every read that
// uses the value as a string (an f-string DSN gets `'**********'`, `hmac.new(settings.SECRET_KEY.encode(), ...)`
// raises), so each needs `.get_secret_value()`. That is why the rule starts in log mode.
// Left alone:
//   - `SecretStr`, `SecretBytes`, `Secret[...]`, a project type deriving from them, and any type that is not a plain
//     string (`int`, `bool`, `list[str]`, `Literal[...]`, a URL or DSN type);
//   - a field its author masked: `Field(repr=False)`, `Annotated[str, PlainSerializer(...)]` or `WrapSerializer` (in
//     place or through an alias such as `MaskedStr`), or a `@field_serializer` naming it (or "*") in its class;
//   - DSN fields (`DATABASE_URL: str`, `REDIS_URL`) even when the URL embeds a password: the name says URL, and a
//     URL often carries none; a gap, not a judgement that it is safe;
//   - request and response models (`password: str` on a login body: input, which the fastapi pack's response rules
//     own), non-Pydantic config classes and dataclasses, pydantic.v1 settings, ClassVar and `_private` attributes;
//   - test code (pd_test_doc), and migrations (a path part `migrations` or `alembic`): a settings class a migration
//     defines reads the environment once for that migration, and is not the process's settings object.
// Overlap: Bandit B105/B106/B107 and Ruff S105-S107 report a hard-coded password literal (`SECRET_KEY: str =
// "changeme"`); this rule is about the type, whatever the default, so both may fire on a literal default.
// Gaps: names whose last word is an abbreviation or a key without a secret word before it (`DB_PASS`, `FERNET_KEY`,
// `OPENAI_KEY`, `ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `SIGNING_KEY`, `SALT`): `_KEY` alone also ends `CACHE_KEY` and `SORT_KEY`; a
// secret word followed by a qualifier (`INNER_API_KEY_FOR_PLUGIN`); a Vault AppRole `SECRET_ID`; a vendor's public
// key named like a secret (PostHog's `POSTHOG_PROJECT_API_KEY`, reported); a quoted annotation (`X_PASSWORD: "str"`);
// a PEP 695 `type` alias; a settings base outside the run that is not a known base;
// pydantic.v1 settings classes; whether the settings object really reaches a log (few code bases print it; the field
// is a leak waiting for the first `logger.info(settings)` or exception report). The read count matches `.NAME` on any
// object, so a lower-case name counts other objects' reads.

#include "lib/pydantic.rerail"

.violation PlaintextSecretSetting(at: node, name: symbol, reads: number) "Declare `{name}` as `SecretStr` and change each read of it to `.{name}.get_secret_value()` ({reads} in this run); a read left as is gets `'**********'`. Keep `str` if it is not a secret."
PlaintextSecretSetting(a, x, n) :- sss_field(x, a, t), sss_str_ann(t), sss_secret(a), !sss_masked(a, x), docof(a, d),
    !pd_test_doc(d), !sss_migration_doc(d), n = count : { attr_of(_, _, x) }.

.decl sss_migration_doc(d: number)
sss_migration_doc(d) :- doc(d, _, _), (path_part(d, "migrations") ; path_part(d, "alembic")).

// ---- the fields --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sss_conf(c): model c is configuration: a settings class, or a model a configuration model holds as a field.
.decl sss_conf(c: node)
sss_conf(c) :- pd_settings(c).
sss_conf(c) :- sss_conf(s), pd_has_field(s, _, _, t), pd_ann_model(t, c), pd_model(c).
// sss_field(x, a, t): field x of a configuration model, declared by a with annotation t (in that class or a base).
.decl sss_field(x: symbol, a: node, t: node)
sss_field(x, a, t) :- sss_conf(c), pd_has_field(c, x, a, t).
// sss_field_call(a, k): k is the `Field(...)` call of field a: its value, or Annotated metadata in its annotation.
.decl sss_field_call(a: node, k: node)
sss_field_call(a, k) :- sss_field(_, a, _), field(a, "right", v), unparen(v, k), pd_field_call(k).
sss_field_call(a, k) :- sss_field(_, a, t), sss_reach(t, e), sss_annotated_meta(e, m),
    (unparen(m, k) ; kind(m, "type"), child(m, c, 0), unparen(c, k)), pd_field_call(k).

// ---- the name ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sss_name(a, y): field a goes by y: its name, or a string alias its Field gives (the environment variable's name).
.decl sss_name(a: node, y: symbol)
sss_name(a, x) :- sss_field(x, a, _).
sss_name(a, y) :- sss_field_call(a, k), (w = "alias" ; w = "validation_alias"), call_arg(k, -1, w, s), str(s, y).
sss_name(a, y) :- sss_field_call(a, k), call_arg(k, -1, "validation_alias", e), unparen(e, c), kind(c, "call"),
    field(c, "function", f), sym_of(f, q), (q = "pydantic.AliasChoices" ; q = "pydantic.aliases.AliasChoices"),
    posarg(c, _, s), str(s, y).
// sss_secret_word(y): the last word part of y names a secret. The parts are cut at `_` (any case) and at camel-case
// humps; a trailing number is not a part. Each pattern matches the whole name.
.decl sss_secret_word(y: symbol)
// snake or upper case: `..._PASSWORD`, `..._SECRET_KEY`, `..._SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `token`, `api_key_2`.
sss_secret_word(y) :- sss_name(_, y),
    match("(?i)(.*_)?(password|passwd|secret|token|credentials?|apikey|pepper)_?[0-9]*", y).
sss_secret_word(y) :- sss_name(_, y), match(
    "(?i)(.*_)?(password|passwd|secret|token|credentials?|apikey|pepper|api|private)(_access)?_key_?[0-9]*", y).
// camel case: `slackBotToken`, `stripeApiKey`, `openaiAPIKey`, `privateKey`, `secretAccessKey`.
sss_secret_word(y) :- sss_name(_, y),
    match("(.*[a-z0-9])?(Password|Passwd|Secret|Token|Credentials?|Apikey|Pepper)[0-9]*", y).
sss_secret_word(y) :- sss_name(_, y),
    match("(.*[a-z0-9])?(Password|Passwd|Secret|Token|Credentials?|Pepper|Api|API|Private)(Access)?Key[0-9]*", y).
sss_secret_word(y) :- sss_name(_, y),
    match("(password|passwd|secret|token|credentials?|pepper|api|private)(Access)?Key[0-9]*", y).
// sss_secret(a): field a's name or one of its aliases ends in a secret.
.decl sss_secret(a: node)
sss_secret(a) :- sss_name(a, y), sss_secret_word(y).

// ---- the annotation ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sss_dom(e): the annotations read, and their parts.
.decl sss_dom(e: node)
sss_dom(t) :- sss_field(_, _, t).
sss_dom(a) :- sss_part(_, a).
// sss_bare(e, m): e without `type` wrappers and parentheses.
.decl sss_strip(e: node)
sss_strip(e) :- sss_dom(e).
sss_strip(c) :- sss_strip(e), unparen(e, t), kind(t, "type"), child(t, c, 0).
.decl sss_bare(e: node, m: node)
sss_bare(e, m) :- sss_strip(e), unparen(e, m), !kind(m, "type").
sss_bare(e, m) :- sss_strip(e), unparen(e, t), kind(t, "type"), child(t, c, 0), sss_bare(c, m).
// sss_sub(e, h, i, a): e is h[...] with a as its i-th element.
.decl sss_sub(e: node, h: node, i: number, a: node)
sss_sub(e, h, i, a) :- sss_bare(e, m), kind(m, "subscript"), field(m, "value", h), field(m, "subscript", a0),
    !kind(a0, "tuple"), i = count : { field(m, "subscript", b), b < a0 }, a = a0.
sss_sub(e, h, i, a) :- sss_bare(e, m), kind(m, "subscript"), field(m, "value", h), field(m, "subscript", t),
    kind(t, "tuple"), count : { field(m, "subscript", _) } = 1, child(t, a, i).
sss_sub(e, h, i, a) :- sss_bare(e, m), kind(m, "generic_type"), child(m, h, 0), child(m, tp, 1),
    kind(tp, "type_parameter"), child(tp, a, i).
.decl sss_typing(h: node, x: symbol)
sss_typing(h, x) :- sym_of(h, q), split_dot(q, m, x), (m = "typing" ; m = "typing_extensions").
// sss_part(e, a): a is a member e is made of: Optional's, Union's and `|`'s members, Annotated's type, and the value
// of the module-level alias a name stands for.
.decl sss_part(e: node, a: node)
sss_part(e, a) :- sss_sub(e, h, _, a), (sss_typing(h, "Optional") ; sss_typing(h, "Union")).
sss_part(e, a) :- sss_sub(e, h, 0, a), sss_typing(h, "Annotated").
sss_part(e, a) :- sss_bare(e, m), (kind(m, "binary_operator"), op(m, "|") ; kind(m, "union_type")), child(m, a, _).
sss_part(e, v) :- sss_bare(e, m), (kind(m, "identifier") ; kind(m, "attribute")), pd_name_value(m, v).
// sss_annotated_meta(e, k): k is metadata of Annotated e (an element after the first), parts included.
.decl sss_annotated_meta(e: node, k: node)
sss_annotated_meta(e, k) :- sss_sub(e, h, i, k), i > 0, sss_typing(h, "Annotated").
// sss_reach(t, e): e is t or one of its parts, at any depth.
.decl sss_reach(t: node, e: node)
sss_reach(t, t) :- sss_field(_, _, t).
sss_reach(t, a) :- sss_reach(t, e), sss_part(e, a).
// sss_plain(e): e is a plain string type or None: builtin `str`, pydantic's StrictStr or `constr(...)`, `None`.
.decl sss_plain(e: node)
sss_plain(e) :- sss_bare(e, m), kind(m, "identifier"), text(m, "str").
sss_plain(e) :- sss_bare(e, m), kind(m, "none").
sss_plain(e) :- sss_bare(e, m), (kind(m, "identifier") ; kind(m, "attribute")), sym_of(m, q), sss_str_type(q).
sss_plain(e) :- sss_bare(e, m), kind(m, "call"), field(m, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "pydantic.constr" ; q = "pydantic.types.constr").
.decl sss_str_type(q: symbol)
sss_str_type("pydantic.StrictStr"). sss_str_type("pydantic.types.StrictStr").
// sss_leaf_other(e): part e is made of nothing smaller, and is not a plain string or None.
.decl sss_leaf_other(e: node)
sss_leaf_other(e) :- sss_dom(e), !sss_part(e, _), !sss_plain(e).
// sss_str_ann(t): annotation t is a plain string, alone or with None.
.decl sss_str_ann(t: node)
sss_str_ann(t) :- sss_reach(t, e), !sss_part(e, _), sss_bare(e, m), !kind(m, "none"), sss_plain(e),
    !sss_has_other(t).
.decl sss_has_other(t: node)
sss_has_other(t) :- sss_reach(t, e), sss_leaf_other(e).

// ---- masked by its author ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sss_masked(a, x): field a (named x) does not print in clear by its author's choice: `Field(repr=False)` as its value
// or as Annotated metadata, a PlainSerializer or WrapSerializer in its Annotated (in place or through an alias), or a
// @field_serializer naming x (or "*") in its class.
.decl sss_masked(a: node, x: symbol)
sss_masked(a, x) :- sss_field(x, a, _), sss_field_call(a, k), sss_repr_false(k).
sss_masked(a, x) :- sss_field(x, a, t), sss_reach(t, e), sss_annotated_meta(e, m), (k = m ; within(k, m)),
    kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", f), sym_of(f, q), sss_serializer(q).
sss_masked(a, x) :- sss_field(x, a, _), nearest(a, c, scope), kind(c, "class_definition"),
    kind(f, "function_definition"), nearest(f, c, scope), decorator(f, e0), unparen(e0, e), kind(e, "call"),
    field(e, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q),
    (q = "pydantic.field_serializer" ; q = "pydantic.functional_serializers.field_serializer"),
    posarg(e, _, s), str(s, y), (y = x ; y = "*").
.decl sss_repr_false(k: node)
sss_repr_false(k) :- call_arg(k, -1, "repr", v), kind(v, "false").
.decl sss_serializer(q: symbol)
sss_serializer("pydantic.PlainSerializer"). sss_serializer("pydantic.WrapSerializer").
sss_serializer("pydantic.functional_serializers.PlainSerializer").
sss_serializer("pydantic.functional_serializers.WrapSerializer").
// The cases, `cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/`, read as one repository: each line ending in `# caught` is
// reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "app/__init__.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/alembic/versions/0002_backfill_ai_provider.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/alembic/versions/0002_backfill_ai_provider.py"
    .fixture "app/core/__init__.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/core/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/core/base.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/core/base.py"
    .fixture "app/core/config.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/core/config.py"
    .fixture "app/core/names.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/core/names.py"
    .fixture "app/core/types.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/core/types.py"
    .fixture "app/legacy.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/legacy.py"
    .fixture "app/plain.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/plain.py"
    .fixture "app/schemas.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/schemas.py"
    .fixture "app/security.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/security.py"
    .fixture "app/worker/__init__.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/worker/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/worker/settings.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/app/worker/settings.py"
    .fixture "pyproject.toml" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/pyproject.toml"
    .fixture "tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "tests/test_config.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-secret-settings-str/tests/test_config.py"
    .expect _ at "app/core/base.py":11
    .expect _ at "app/core/base.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/core/base.py":26
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":14
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":15
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":16
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":17
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":19
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":20
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":21
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":22
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":24
    .expect _ at "app/core/config.py":72
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":11
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":12
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":13
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":14
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":15
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":16
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":17
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":19
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":20
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":21
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":24
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":25
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":26
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":27
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":28
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":31
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":32
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":33
    .expect _ at "app/core/names.py":55
    .expect _ at "app/worker/settings.py":7
    .expect PlaintextSecretSetting(_, "POSTGRES_PASSWORD", 1)
    .expect PlaintextSecretSetting(_, "SECRET_KEY", 2)
.end
